---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How it works — CanYouDo?">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
      <h1>Clear roles. Fair money. No small print surprises.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--ink-600)">CanYouDo? is an <strong>introduction service</strong>: an online notice board that connects you with independent local cleaners and handles the boring bits — bookings, reminders, messaging and ratings.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px">For customers</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><strong>Browse cleaners</strong> by area and availability. Every profile shows their services, their insurer, and their measurable track record: punctuality rate, completion rate and average rating.</li>
        <li><strong>Book online.</strong> Pick a date, time and number of hours, and list exactly which areas you want cleaned. Our AI-assisted booking system checks the details and sends automatic email confirmations to both of you.</li>
        <li><strong>Pay two ways, transparently.</strong> You pay CanYouDo? a <strong>£5/hour introduction fee</strong> online when you book. You pay your cleaner <strong>£15/hour directly</strong> (cash or bank transfer) on the day. Total: £20/hour, and you always know where every pound went.</li>
        <li><strong>Provide the products.</strong> You supply all cleaning products and equipment. Your cleaner brings the skill. This keeps things simple, hygienic and yours to control.</li>
        <li><strong>Rate what matters.</strong> After each visit you answer quick, factual questions: Were they on time? Did they clean the areas you asked for? Did they follow your instructions? These scores drive your cleaner's bonus — honest ratings directly reward great work.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px">For cleaners</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><strong>Sign up and build your profile.</strong> Add your services, the area you cover, your weekly availability, and your public liability insurance details (insurer, policy number, expiry). Insurance is your responsibility as an independent provider — profiles display an "Insured" badge once details are added.</li>
        <li><strong>Get booked.</strong> Customers book you through the site. You'll see every job in your portal and get an email the moment a booking comes in. Confirm or decline — your diary, your call.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep £15 of every £20.</strong> Customers pay you £15/hour directly. No waiting for payouts, no commission taken from your rate.</li>
        <li><strong>Earn bonuses for measurable quality.</strong> Each month, cleaners with consistently great scores earn cash bonuses funded from the introduction fee: up to <strong>£50/month</strong> for perfect punctuality, completed checklists and top ratings.</li>
        <li><strong>Message clients from your portal.</strong> Running late? Need access details? Chat with your customers per booking, with everything in one place.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px">What CanYouDo? does — and doesn't do</h2>
      <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top:20px">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>We do</h3>
          <ul class="check-list" style="margin:0">
            <li>Introduce customers to independent cleaners</li>
            <li>Run the booking system, reminders &amp; emails</li>
            <li>Host messaging and factual ratings</li>
            <li>Pay quality bonuses to cleaners</li>
            <li>Provide customer support for the platform</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>We don't</h3>
          <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;line-height:2">
            <li>Employ cleaners or supervise their work</li>
            <li>Provide cleaning services ourselves</li>
            <li>Insure the work — cleaners hold their own public liability cover, and customers insure their own homes</li>
            <li>Handle the cleaner's £15/hour — that's paid directly to them</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:36px">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/find-a-cleaner/">Find a cleaner</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/signup/?role=cleaner" style="margin-left:10px">Become a cleaner</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
